  "question": "Let $\\vec{p}$ and $\\vec{q}$ be unit vectors such that $\\vec{p} + \\vec{q}$ is also a unit vector. What is the value of $\\vec{p} \\cdot \\vec{q}$?",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Let $|\\vec{p}| = |\\vec{q}| = 1$ and $|\\vec{p}+\\vec{q}|=1$.<br /><br />$|\\vec{p}+\\vec{q}|^2=(\\vec{p}+\\vec{q})\\cdot(\\vec{p}+\\vec{q})$.<br /><br />$=|\\vec{p}|^2+2\\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{q}+|\\vec{q}|^2$.<br /><br />$=1+2\\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{q}+1=2+2\\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{q}$.<br /><br />Since $|\\vec{p}+\\vec{q}|^2=1$, we get $2+2\\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{q}=1$.<br /><br />$2\\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{q}=-1 \\Rightarrow \\vec{p}\\cdot\\vec{q}=-\\frac{1}{2}$.",
